@*
    The /selftest route with the providers it needs, as a component a host can root on directly.

    Some hosts can navigate to a route at startup and some cannot: MAUI set BlazorWebView.StartPath,
    while Photino's PhotinoBlazorApp loads "/" itself and ignores PhotinoWindow.StartUrl. Rather than
    each host inventing its own way of getting to the probes, a host that cannot navigate roots on
    this instead.

    It is EmptyLayout's four providers and SelfTest, and it exists for the same reason EmptyLayout
    does: MainLayout would start the whole application - loading the last project, formatting modified
    files, kicking off analysis - underneath the probes, and a host comparison has to compare the host
    rather than whatever a library happened to be doing at the time.

    Routing is not left untested by this. The host resolves "/" through the router in its ordinary
    mode, which is how it starts at all.
*@

<MudThemeProvider />
<MudPopoverProvider />
<MudDialogProvider />
<MudSnackbarProvider />

<SelfTest />
